Group Anagrams
Problem Description

Given an array of strings strs, group the anagrams together. You can return the answer in any order.

An anagram is a word formed by rearranging the letters of another word, using all the original letters exactly once.

Approach: Sorting + Hash Map

The solution uses a hash map (defaultdict) to group strings that are anagrams.

How It Works
Initialize a dictionary using defaultdict(list).
Iterate through each string in the input list.
Sort the characters of the current string to generate a unique key.
Join the sorted characters to form a string key.
Append the original string to the dictionary entry corresponding to that key.
Return all grouped anagrams using list(ans.values()).

Since anagrams contain the same characters, their sorted versions will be identical.


Example

Input:

python
strs = ["eat", "tea", "tan", "ate", "nat", "bat"]


Output:

python
[["eat", "tea", "ate"], ["tan", "nat"], ["bat"]]


Explanation:

"eat", "tea", and "ate" share the sorted key "aet".
"tan" and "nat" share the sorted key "ant".
"bat" has the sorted key "abt".

Therefore, all anagrams are grouped together.

Complexity Analysis

Let:

N = number of strings.
K = maximum length of a string.
Operation	Complexity
Sorting each string	O(K log K)
Processing all strings	O(N × K log K)
Hash map insertion	O(N) expected
Overall Time	O(N × K log K)
Space Complexity	O(N × K)
